From: Trijal Saha <97483939+Trijal08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] samsung-sit: stop polling the call list

The generic voice interface polls GET_CALL_LIST on a timer unless the
modem says it reports call state by itself. The CP does report it --
CALL_STATE_CHANGED arrives unsolicited and already drives
mm_iface_modem_voice_reload_all_calls() -- but nothing ever set the flag,
so the timer ran the whole time.

Measured against the capture, 220s span, no calls placed on either side:
20 GET_CALL_LIST requests from us against 4 from stock, 17 of ours on ch
0xf5 alone.

The reason it was never set is that the generic code decides it in
clcc_format_check_ready(), which hangs off the +CLCC probe inside the AT
check_support -- and this plugin replaces check_support entirely, because
there is no capability query for the SIT call group. So the property kept
its polling default and the AT path that would have cleared it never ran.
Set it where the override lives.
diff -ruN a/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-broadband-modem-samsung-sit.c b/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-broadband-modem-samsung-sit.c
--- a/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-broadband-modem-samsung-sit.c	2026-11-08 09:02:12.666249245 -0500
+++ b/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-broadband-modem-samsung-sit.c	2026-11-08 11:47:26.914353790 -0500
@@ -6429,6 +6429,23 @@
 
     /* Every SIT CP speaks the CS call group; there is no capability query
      * for it, and the port is the same one already in use. */
+
+    /*
+     * And no call-list polling. The generic interface polls GET_CALL_LIST on a
+     * timer unless told the modem reports call state on its own, and the CP
+     * does: CALL_STATE_CHANGED arrives unsolicited and
+     * mm_iface_modem_voice_reload_all_calls() already runs from it.
+     *
+     * The AT path that would normally decide this never runs here, because it
+     * hangs off the +CLCC probe in the check_support we are replacing, so the
+     * property keeps its polling default. Measured cost of that default
+     * against the capture: 20 GET_CALL_LIST requests in 220s where stock
+     * sends 4.
+     */
+    g_object_set (self,
+                  MM_IFACE_MODEM_VOICE_PERIODIC_CALL_LIST_CHECK_DISABLED, TRUE,
+                  NULL);
+
     task = g_task_new (self, NULL, callback, user_data);
     g_task_return_boolean (task, TRUE);
     g_object_unref (task);
